  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0126d7c6e9586af4b99c87708fd95382, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: Coal Face B, east shaft. Morning rotation. Going home to the east block.
    midDaysAnswer: C shaft. They sealed the east one. Eleven hours. Longer walk home.
    finalDaysAnswer: Nowhere. The mine is shut. I stood at the gate a while.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: The tram depot. I drive the number four line. Twelve years now.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Coal Face B, east shaft. Same as always. Nothing to report.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: The station. Wife left on the Tbilisi train. I live alone now.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  - question: Are you experiencing any symptoms?
    earlyDaysAnswer: Coal dust. Always coal dust. The mine doctor says my lungs are fine.
    midDaysAnswer: Some dizziness. Ventilation in C shaft is bad. It passes. Mostly.
    finalDaysAnswer: Tired. More than usual. No sleep without the shift. Same cough.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Nothing. I am thirty-one. The body does not complain yet.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Nothing. C shaft has the best air in the mine. New fans.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Never coughed in my life. I kept the office ledgers. Never went down.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - B shaft today. Long one. Papers are in order. Always are.
    - I know I smell. The showers at the mine were out again.
    midDays:
    - Three men on my crew did not show this morning. Nobody said anything.
    - I do not complain. I just want to get through the week.
    finalDays:
    - The mine is closed. First time in thirty years I have nothing to go back to.
    - Just going home. That is all there is now.
